  {
   "id": "intro",
   "type": "intro",
   "heading": {
    "en": "The life table",
    "kn": "ಜೀವನ ಕೋಷ್ಟಕ"
   },
   "hook": {
    "en": "How does an insurance company decide that a 25-year-old pays a smaller premium than a 55-year-old? It reads a life table.",
    "kn": "25 ವರ್ಷದವರು 55 ವರ್ಷದವರಿಗಿಂತ ಕಡಿಮೆ ವಿಮಾ ಕಂತು ಕಟ್ಟಬೇಕು ಎಂದು ವಿಮಾ ಕಂಪನಿ ಹೇಗೆ ನಿರ್ಧರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ? ಅದು ಜೀವನ ಕೋಷ್ಟಕವನ್ನು ಓದುತ್ತದೆ."
   },
   "objectives": [
    {
     "en": "State the assumptions and uses of a life table"
    },
    {
     "en": "Define the columns lₓ, dₓ, qₓ, pₓ, Lₓ, Tₓ, eₓ⁰"
    },
    {
     "en": "Construct a life table and find expectation of life"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "How does an insurance company decide that a 25-year-old pays a smaller premium than a 55-year-old? It reads a life table.",
    "kn": "25 ವರ್ಷದವರು 55 ವರ್ಷದವರಿಗಿಂತ ಕಡಿಮೆ ವಿಮಾ ಕಂತು ಕಟ್ಟಬೇಕು ಎಂದು ವಿಮಾ ಕಂಪನಿ ಹೇಗೆ ನಿರ್ಧರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ? ಅದು ಜೀವನ ಕೋಷ್ಟಕವನ್ನು ಓದುತ್ತದೆ."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Life table: meaning and assumptions"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "A life table follows a cohort of persons (say 1,00,000 or 1000) born at the same time until all of them die, giving at each age the number alive and the probability of dying. Assumptions: the cohort is closed (no migration), deaths occur only according to the age-specific mortality, and deaths are spread uniformly within each year of age. Uses: insurance premiums, comparison of longevity, population projection, public health planning."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Cohort (radix) l₀ = 1000 or 1,00,000"
    },
    {
     "en": "Closed group: no migration"
    },
    {
     "en": "Uniform deaths within a year"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "A life table follows a group of people born together until all of them die. It assumes a closed group and deaths spread evenly within each year.",
    "kn": "ಜೀವನ ಕೋಷ್ಟಕವು ಒಟ್ಟಿಗೆ ಹುಟ್ಟಿದ ಗುಂಪನ್ನು ಎಲ್ಲರೂ ಸಾಯುವವರೆಗೆ ಅನುಸರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ಮುಚ್ಚಿದ ಗುಂಪು ಮತ್ತು ವರ್ಷದೊಳಗೆ ಮರಣಗಳು ಸಮವಾಗಿ ಹರಡಿವೆ ಎಂದು ಊಹಿಸುತ್ತದೆ."
   }
  },
